## Working protocol: sessions, plan, progress

Context is limited and compaction loses detail, so state lives in files, not in the chat.

- `PLAN.md` is the ordered task list. Each task is small enough for one subagent run.
- `PROGRESS.md` is **generated** by `scripts/progress.mjs` from `PLAN.md` and `progress/`. It shows the next
  task, open notes, decisions and the recent log. **Never edit `PROGRESS.md`, `PLAN.md` ticks, or `progress/`
  by hand.** The script is the only writer:

  ```bash
  node scripts/progress.mjs                                   # regenerate, print Next and open notes
  node scripts/progress.mjs done <id> --summary "<one line>" --files "<a.ts, b.css>" \
       --decisions "<one line or omit>" --open "<one line or omit>"   # task finished: ticks PLAN.md
  node scripts/progress.mjs note "<text>"                     # follow-up or review item
  node scripts/progress.mjs resolve <n>                       # an open note is dealt with
  node scripts/progress.mjs decision "<text>"                 # lasting choice later tasks must respect
  node scripts/progress.mjs check                             # fails if anything has drifted
  ```
- **Who records what:** the `implementer` subagent runs `done` for its task. The main chat never runs `done`
  and never edits `PLAN.md` or `PROGRESS.md`; it only reads them. If `check` fails, run the command it names.
- **At session start:** run `node scripts/progress.mjs`, read the task named as Next in `PLAN.md`, and handle
  any open note that blocks it. Do not re-explore the whole repo.
- **HARD STOP after two completed tasks.** When the second task of this session is done (its subagent has
  returned and recorded it with `done`), STOP. Do not start a third task, not even a small one. Your final
  message is: what was done, what is next, and "Run `/clear`, then say: read PROGRESS.md and continue."
  Stop earlier, after one task, if the session has needed many retries or long investigations. Never rely on
  `/compact` or auto-compaction; the files are the memory.

## Subagents: keep the main chat small

The main chat plans, delegates, and integrates. Heavy work happens in subagents, whose file reads and tool output never enter the main context.

- Use the **`implementer`** agent for each `PLAN.md` task: give it the task, the files involved, and which `docs/` sections apply.
- Use the **`test-runner`** agent (it also runs `progress.mjs check`) to run {{CHECK_NAMES: e.g. typecheck, lint, test, build}} and report failures.
- Subagents reply in **15 lines or fewer**: files changed, checks run and their result, open issues. They never paste whole files or diffs back.
- Run subagents one at a time. This box serves one request at a time, so parallel subagents only queue.
- Do the work yourself, without a subagent, when it is a one-line fix or a question about a file already in context.

## Context hygiene

- Find before you read: `grep -n` or Glob first, then read only the line range you need.
- Never `cat` or Read a whole large file to look for one thing.
- Pipe long command output through `tail`, e.g. {{EXAMPLE_TRIMMED_COMMAND: `npm run build 2>&1 | tail -40`}}.
- Do not Read images or screenshots: the model may be text-only, and an image in context breaks every later request. Check rendered output with DOM queries or pixel reads in a script instead.
- Visual checks are done by the human. Say what to look at; do not claim to have seen it.

